# UI and Forms

## Components

- Prefer **small, reusable components** — avoid copy-paste. Share layout and patterns through composition and existing `components/ui` (shadcn).
- Match project styling: Tailwind v4, BazaarPrinting CSS tokens (`var(--color-bg)`, `var(--color-text-muted)`, etc. — never hardcoded hex), accessible focus states.
- All interactive elements must have a visible focus style — use `outline`, `box-shadow`, or `border-color` keyed to `var(--color-accent)`.

## Motion and affordance

- Add tasteful **hover**, **focus-visible**, and **transition** on interactive elements (buttons, links, cards acting as controls). Keep motion subtle.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` when adding non-trivial animation — wrap keyframe animations in `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference)`.
- Button active state: `transform: scale(0.97)`. Hover: `opacity: 0.9`. No heavy shadows or bounces.

## Inputs and validation

- Use correct **HTML input types** (`email`, `number`, `tel`, `url`, `password`) and meaningful `autoComplete` values.
- **Phone and email fields** must use `PhoneInput` and `EmailInput` from `components/ui/` — see `form-inputs` rule.
- Add validation aligned to the field: email format, min/max/step for numbers, required fields, length limits.
- Surface errors **next to the field** using the field-level `error` prop — not a single banner for the whole form.
- Use `aria-invalid` and `aria-describedby` on inputs when showing errors.
- Prefer shared validation helpers from `lib/utils/` once introduced; keep validation consistent per screen until then.

## Labels

All form labels follow the design system style:
- `12px / font-weight 500 / uppercase / letter-spacing: 0.06em`
- Color: `var(--color-text-muted)`
- Always use `<label htmlFor="...">` — never skip labels for accessibility

## Error display

```tsx
{error && (
  <p
    id="field-error"
    className="mt-1.5 text-[12px] font-medium"
    style={{ color: "var(--color-danger)" }}
    role="alert"
  >
    {error}
  </p>
)}
<input aria-invalid={!!error} aria-describedby={error ? "field-error" : undefined} ... />
```
